# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working docs, notes and context — local only, never committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything above this block is a DENYLIST OF EXACT FILENAMES, added reactively
# one name at a time. That shape cannot hold: a working note is tracked by
# default until somebody remembers to add its exact name here, and the rule only
# ever arrives after the file already exists. It also does nothing to a file that
# is already tracked -- `.gitignore` does not untrack -- which is how
# `nucleus/PARITY-COMPARISON.md` sat public on the GitHub mirror from 2026-07-20
# while both the ignore list and the document's own first line called it
# local-only.
#
# The patterns below are CONVENTIONS instead: name a note in any of these shapes
# and it is ignored the moment it is created, without an edit here. Prefer them
# for anything new.
#
# `.github/scripts/check_ignored_not_tracked.py` enforces the whole file: it
# fails if any tracked path matches an ignore rule, so intent and reality cannot
# drift apart again silently.

# Private planning trees. `_internal/` is its own private git repo (Forgejo
# `Tyler/neutron-internal`) — gitignored here so the public repo never sees it,
# versioned there so it is not single-copy on one laptop.
/_internal/
**/_internal/
**/_notes/
**/_scratch/
**/.notes/

# Note/context/session filename conventions
**/INTERNAL.md
**/NOTES.md
**/*_NOTES.md
**/*-NOTES.md
**/NOTES-*.md
**/SESSION_*.md
**/SESSION-*.md
**/HANDOFF*.md
**/*_HANDOFF.md
**/SCRATCH*.md
**/WIP*.md
**/DRAFT*.md
**/TODO.md
**/TODO-*.md
**/BRAINSTORM*.md
**/RESEARCH-*.md
**/*-RESEARCH.md
**/POSTMORTEM*.md
**/RETRO*.md
**/DECISIONS.md
**/OPEN_WORK.md
**/PROGRESS.md
**/ORCHESTRATION.md
**/GROUND_TRUTH.md

# The universal escape hatch: any file may be made local-only by adding `.local`
# before its extension. Use this instead of extending the denylist above.
**/*.local.md
**/*.local.txt
**/*.local.json
**/*.local.*

uv.lock

